Electron interactions, magnetism and superconductivity — Daniel C. Ralph (@mat-ralph-magnetism: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mat-sources) { r_3B28YDT2Z6KYBRZ8DHM1069TW1
Daniel C. Ralph, Cornell University, 2024. [Version and metadata](https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.11169v1), [89-page graduate notes](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2408.11169), [CC BY 4.0 licence](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

Read all seven sections and the attached homework. Begin with the many-electron basis and the approximations motivating a model Hamiltonian; follow magnetic instability, applications, pairing and superconducting response. The text expects prior quantum/statistical work. Its first section can be revisited after an initial model-based reading, as the author suggests.

Metadata, contents and selected exchange, Stoner and superconducting length-scale passages were inspected on 30 October 2026. This provides graduate depth beyond the unavailable MIT magnetic unit. A model or review of an application does not certify the performance of a commercial material. Preserve version, attribution and component credits; the PDF remains external.

